{
  "name": "pollis-toolbox-smart-regions",
  "displayName": "Smart Regions Toolbox",
  "description": "Pollis Smart Regions Toolbox: spatiotemporal infrastructure, pollution and climate, for municipalities and regional authorities in Smart Cities and Smart Rural Areas. Reads GeoJSON, GeoPackage, Shapefile, GeoParquet, FlatGeobuf, KML and GPX files through DuckDB's spatial extension, reads GeoTIFF rasters, LAS and LAZ lidar point clouds, CityGML and CityJSON 3D city models, GTFS transit feeds and OpenStreetMap PBF extracts, reads the features of OpenStreetMap with a tag in an area from the Overpass API, and the layers or the full extract of a region from Geofabrik's download server, reads the places, buildings, roads, boundaries and addresses of an area from Overture Maps, reads the NUTS regions, local administrative units, countries and Urban Audit cities of Eurostat GISCO and maps Eurostat's tables on them, finds the INSPIRE datasets of administrative and statistical units in data.europa.eu and reads them from the countries' WFS, Atom feeds and OGC API Features, finds the Sentinel scenes of an area in the STAC catalogue of the Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem and downloads the bands of a Sentinel-2 scene or of a Sentinel-1 monthly mosaic, finds the scenes of a dataset of USGS EarthExplorer through its Machine-to-Machine API and downloads the bands of a Landsat 8-9 scene or the SRTM elevation of an area, finds the lidar surveys and elevation models of an area in the catalogue of OpenTopography and downloads the elevation of an area from a global model or from the 3D Elevation Program of the U.S. Geological Survey, reads the street-level images of an area from the coverage tiles and image search of Mapillary, with their thumbnails and the map features located from them, shows them on OpenStreetMap base maps, tests a value of a set of areas for spatial autocorrelation with Moran's I and Local Moran (LISA), and maps a value measured at stations with variograms, kriging, inverse distance weighting and Gaussian simulation.",
  "version": "0.1.22",
  "publisher": "pollis",
  "author": "Pollis",
  "license": "AGPL-3.0",
  "icon": "icon.png",
  "repository": {
    "type": "git",
    "url": "https://github.com/saragga/pollis"
  },
  "engines": {
    "vscode": "*"
  },
